# =============================================================================
# .github/CODEOWNERS — who reviews what (SEC-25, T-26; U-9)
# Source: Docs/dev-team/architecture/infrastructure.md v0.3 §3.2 (F-7, T-012).
# =============================================================================
# The owner is the only human reviewer of three virtual teams, so the base rule
# covers the whole repository. The "contract" directories are then repeated one
# by one: a rule that exists on its own does not get lost when a subdirectory
# is added, and the list is what a reader of a pull request sees named.
#
# Branch protection (set in the repository settings, not here):
#   * main               — required checks + "Require review from Code Owners";
#   * integration/mvp-1  — required checks only. GitHub does not let an author
#                          approve their own pull request, so requiring the
#                          owner's approval on the integration branch would
#                          block the owner (§3.2).
#
# services/_archive/** is deliberately ownerless: the archive is frozen code
# kept for reference (U-1, F-3), and a review request on it is noise.
# =============================================================================

*                    @alekseizabelin1985-spec

# Data the agents obey: prompts, laws and limits. A change here changes the
# behaviour of the swarm without touching a line of Go (T-26).
/blueprints/         @alekseizabelin1985-spec
/laws/               @alekseizabelin1985-spec
/config/             @alekseizabelin1985-spec

# Contracts between the three teams: the event schemas and the shared packages.
/schemas/            @alekseizabelin1985-spec
/shared/             @alekseizabelin1985-spec

# The supply chain: images, pins and the workflows themselves.
/build/              @alekseizabelin1985-spec
/.github/            @alekseizabelin1985-spec
/docker-compose.yml  @alekseizabelin1985-spec
/Makefile            @alekseizabelin1985-spec

# Frozen code, no owner.
/services/_archive/
